From f17e3217b21cc85b205c254ef06cd272862180ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:23:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] nx2: passthrough backend: stale texture headers
 (washed-out race frames), upload store on, keyed video memory

Washed-out race frames (sole mode, 2-15% of shots in every configuration; Vulkan
none): MKW rewrites 80-200 texture headers a frame all through its 4 MiB header
pool, and the pool's shadow pages were refreshed from guest memory at most every
100 ms, so the host sampled stale headers for several frames. A pool scanner
thread (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_POOL_SCAN_US, 2000; 0 off) compares the pools with
its own copy and queues changed pages; the entry thread translates just those
before the next submission. Full refreshes compare in place. 0 washed in 924
shots since (was ~7%).

Upload store v2, on by default in sole mode (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_BACK_UPLOADS=1:
off): Eglantine's back no longer writes compute inline uploads or inline QMDs to
guest memory; the host writes them in stream order (inline QMDs at their guest
address, the guest's words, I2M registers restored). The translator's store words
are stamped with their submission and land once a WFI fence and an L2 flush
passed (shadow-page words written back then); the back's own reads use a back
map. Program reads drain with WFI fences and an L2 flush (DrainFlushed). Fixes
boot hangs where a barrier QMD the back wrote late was copied empty by the host.

Video memory for GPU-only regions is keyed by the guest memory it stands for:
aliases and remaps share it (6956 of 7925 MKW mappings were remaps of guest
memory that had video memory), ~1.6 GiB less VRAM.

Measuring: EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_WASHED (per-frame crop luminance, events before
a washed frame), _POOL_MS, _QMD_HOSTWRITE, STAMPS=2 and QMD/semaphore stamps,
dependence counters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
